  "attestation": "Compact review records (req.records.compact-review) and the chain check (req.records.chain-check). dispatch.mjs: recordDispatch stores the prompt blocks sharedBlocks finds (instructions before \"Reply with JSON only\"; an alignment review's chapter plan; each >= 512 chars) once in verification/parts/<sha256>.json and keeps bundle.promptParts; the logged bundleHash and recordHash are over the whole record as it reads (unchanged values). expandDispatch puts the prompt back and throws on a missing/altered part, a prompt not hashing to bundleHash, or prompt+promptParts together; readDispatches (only direct record files), loadDispatch and readDispatchFile read through it, and every direct reader in obligations.mjs, history.mjs and spine_review.mjs now uses them, so a compact record gives the same answers as the whole record and an unreadable one fails closed as a missing record (dispatch-record-missing, review not counted). shipped.mjs exempts hash-named parts as harness records; site_export/import/handback carry them unchanged inside verification/. records_check.mjs + lib/records/records_check.mjs: read-only CLI over verifyLog/verifyExtends, either layout, unreadable input is a problem. Docs: deliverables.md, PROCEDURE.md, README.md, CHANGELOG.md; REQUIREMENTS.json adds both requirements. Tests verdict-path and redteam-r6-instructor now read records through loadDispatch/readDispatchFile. Reviewed every required item (none of the other listed docs, templates, site or v0.12 scripts needed a change). Tests: the 36 required tests, plus records-compact, records-check, verdict-path and redteam-r6-instructor (613 passed), and the 23 test files that touch verification records (284 passed), all with COURSEWERK_FRAMES=installed, concurrency 2.",
